From da3761138b80c294cc6908e039ac2069a73f6455 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:19:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban chat waits: rewording does not reset
 escalation; exempt ask wakes are bounded

Adversarial review of the previous head: the repeat-park premise hashed the
question (why/reason), so a worker rewording its re-ask after an orchestrator
"not yet" never escalated, and with asks exempt from the wake budget that
woke the orchestrator 8 times in 16 minutes.

- premise_hash: a chat wait's premise is kind + gateway (the orchestrator it
  waits on), declared, reclassified or inferred, so the third chat park in a
  row escalates at REPARK_LIMIT whatever its wording.
- kanban_unloaded: the budget exemption is once per chat and card per hour
  (_ask_exempt_ok); later asks in that hour take the normal budget.
- A declared chat wait with no probe and no clock_only was refused by the
  long-park guard before its comment probe existed (tool and CLI): it is now
  passed as a timed park, and park_probe adds the probe in the txn.

Tests: reworded re-asks escalate on the third park; a declared chat wait parks
with no probe or clock flag and gets the comment probe; the exemption is once
per card per hour. 3 of 53 fail on the previous head; 18 neighbouring files
(468 tests) pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
